# Proposed (milestone2.md, "BallVector": bv_mul_pow2_k, "the same kernel along the entries, with ec true
# only when it is for every entry"). Not readable by the generator as it is: a ball vector of
# gen/kernels has a step that returns the center only and the state of one fold of maxima of the
# centers written (architecture.md, "Ball vectors"). This one needs, besides, a mask of each entry (the
# step's second output, that its scaling was exact) and-ed into a third group of the state, which the
# radius takes; and its radius kernel's claim is not in the vocabulary (bv_mul_pow2_radius.kernel).
# bv_proposals.py runs it by composing its kernels with the interpreter, as the generated code would.
fold:          bv_mul_pow2_2
arrays:        stored x = x0 x1
scalars:       stored rx, supplied c
state:         m, mask ok, mask ex
step:          (z, e) = bv_mul_pow2_step_2(x, c)
record:        (m, ok) = norm_step_2(m, ok, z)
record:        ex = and(ex, e)
combine:       (m, ok) = norm_combine(m, ok, m, ok)
combine:       ex = and(ex, ex)
radius:        rz = bv_mul_pow2_radius(m, ex, rx, c)
finish:        (r, finite) = norm_finish_1(rz, ok)
orders:        sequential, lanes
writes:        z = z0 z1
output:        r
output:        mask finite
value:         x*c
requires:      ball_vector x rx
requires:      power_of_two c
ensures:       encloses_entries z r x*c x=x,rx flag=finite finite_when=abs_le((abs(x)+rx)*c,-2) radii_when=abs_le(rx*c,-2) exact_when=zero_or_abs_gt(x[0]*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(x[1]*c,eta/(2*u));zero_or_abs_gt(rx*c,eta/(2*u))
min_precision: 2
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
